cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, please cite this repository and the Lean name of the result you use."
type: software
title: "Ingham's theorem in Lean: zero-free regions of ζ and the error term in ψ(x)"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked proof, in Lean 4 with Mathlib and PrimeNumberTheoremAnd, of Ingham's theorem
  in both directions: for 1/2 ≤ θ < 1, the Riemann zeta function has no zeros with real part
  greater than θ exactly when ψ(x) = x + O(x^{θ+δ}) for every δ > 0. Corollaries: the Riemann
  hypothesis is equivalent to a square-root error term, and a zero-free region Re s > 7/8 is
  equivalent to ψ(x) = x + O(x^{7/8+δ}). No sorry; only Lean's standard axioms.
